    "title": "Jessica Fox Undergoes Kidney Tumor Surgery",
    "text": "• Triple Olympic gold medalist Jessica Fox has undergone surgery to remove a tumor from her left kidney.\n• Fox announced she will not compete in the remaining canoe-kayak World Cup events this year.\n• The 31-year-old Australian athlete has won gold medals in the K1 and C1 races at the 2024 Paris Olympics and the C1 at the 2020 Tokyo Olympics.\n• Fox is the first female canoe slalomist to win three Olympic gold medals and holds a total of six Olympic medals, the most of any athlete in the sport.\n• In a statement, Fox expressed positivity about her recovery and plans to focus on getting back on the water.\n• The statement from Paddle Australia did not specify whether the tumor was cancerous but confirmed that the surgery was successful.\n• Fox experienced some post-surgery complications but is now recovering well and in good spirits.\n• Australian Olympic Committee president Ian Chesterman acknowledged the difficult time for Fox and her support crew, praising her resilience and determination.",
